    "https://schema.org/mainContentOfPage": [
      {
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tTraditional Symphony SPLASH! (SOLD OUT GRANDSTAND)\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t3 August 2025 @ 7:30 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThe evening you’ve been waiting for is finally here—half a decade later! Victoria’s iconic night of symphonic music returns to a floating barge in the Inner Harbour.\nLed by VS Principal Pops Conductor Sean O’Loughlin, this celebratory program features highlights from past SPLASH! events. From Tobin Stokes Inner Harbour Overture and Holst’s Jupiter from The Planets, to music from Star Wars, E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial and other favorites, the concert builds to the beloved spectacular grand finale with Tchaikovsky’s 1812 Overture and Amazing Grace—complete with fireworks!\nSymphony SPLASH! is a free public event. Please note Grandstand tickets are SOLD OUT.\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n    \n    Meet the ArtistsFull Concert Program\n    \n    \n        \n    \n         Sean O’Loughlin, conductor\nSean O’Loughlin is the Principal Pops Conductor of the Victoria Symphony and the Principal Pops Conductor of Symphoria in Syracuse, NY. As a composer and arranger, his music is characterized by vibrant rhythms, passionate melodies, and colorful scoring. Commissions from the Boston Pops Orchestra, the Los Angeles Philharmonic and the Hollywood Bowl Orchestra highlight and showcase his diverse musical abilities. As a conductor, he has led performances with the Boston Pops Orchestra, the San Francisco Symphony, the Chicago Symphony, the Hollywood Bowl Orchestra, the Minnesota Orchestra, the Dallas Symphony, the Vancouver Symphony, the Atlanta Symphony, the Baltimore Symphony, the Houston Symphony and the Seattle Symphony amongst others. He has served as conductor for international tours with Josh Groban, Sarah McLachlan and the Jerry Garcia Symphonic Celebration. He has also appeared on ABC’s Good Morning America with Josh Groban and NBC’s “A Very Pentatonix Christmas.”\nRecent collaborations include such artists as Sarah McLachlan, Adele, Josh Groban, Pentatonix, Steven Tyler and Joe Perry, Kelly Clarkson, Diana Ross, Journey, Melissa Etheridge, Blue Man Group, Janelle Monáe, Audra McDonald, Hall and Oates, Gloria Estefan, the Indigo Girls, Diana Krall, Itzhak Perlman, Natalie Merchant, Chris Isaak, Pink Martini, Brandi Carlile, The Decemberists and others.\nThrough his growing number of commissioned and published works, Sean is excited to continue contributing to the rich history of orchestral and wind band literature. His music is published by Excelcia Music, Hal Leonard and Carl Fischer. He is a frequent guest conductor with professional orchestras and honor bands around the country. An annual ASCAP Special Awards winner, Sean was a composition fellow at the Henry Mancini Institute in Los Angeles, and holds composition degrees from New England Conservatory and Syracuse University.\n\nPatrick Cao, piano\nBorn in Nanaimo, BC, in 2011, Patrick Cao is currently a Grade 9 student in Royal Bay Secondary school (French Immersion) in Victoria BC.\nPatrick began studying piano at the age of 3 and a half years old, and at the age of 9 he had already passed the RCM piano level 10 exam. When his family moved to Victoria in 2018, he continued his piano studies with University of Victoria Professor of piano, Arthur Rowe.\nPatrick has been a laureate in many competitions. He has been a frequent winner in several GVPAF (Greater Victoria Performing Arts Festival) classes for several years. In 2022 he won 1st place in the Canada West Performing Arts Festival in the 12 & under category, as well as 2nd place in the Don Chrysler (Sooke Orchestra) Concerto Competition. In 2023 he took 1st place in the Don Chrysler competition, and performed Mendelssohn’s 2nd piano concerto with the Sooke Philharmonic Orchestra, conducted by Yariv Aloni.\nIn March of 2025 Patrick was invited to audition at the renowned Curtis School of Music in Philadelphia, and this summer he looks forward to his first performances with the Victoria Symphony, at Butchart Gardens and at Symphony Splash, with a movement of Tchaikovsky’s first piano concerto.\n\n    \n\n    \n        O Canada \nInner Harbour Overture  Tobin Stokes \nFestive Overture in A major Shostakovich \nSymphony No. 41 in C major, “Jupiter”, IV. Molto allegro  Mozart \nEnigma Variations, IX. “Nimrod”  Elgar \nPiano Concerto No. 1 in B-flat minor, III. Allegro con fuoco  Tchaikovsky\nSabre Dance from Gayane  Khachaturian \nThe Planets, “Jupiter”  Holst\nIntermission\nStar Wars Main Title   John Williams \n“Cantina Band” from Star Wars  John Williams, arr. Christian Ramin\nOn the Beautiful Blue Danube – Excerpt   J. Strauss Jr\nHow To Train Your Dragon  John Powell, arr. Sean O’Loughlin\n“Adventures on Earth” from E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial  John Williams \n1812 Overture  Tchaikovsky \nAmazing Grace  Traditional,  arr. Sean O’Loughlin\n\n    \n\n    \n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAdd to calendar\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tGoogle Calendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tiCalendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook 365\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook Live\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t 3 August 2025 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tstarts at 7:30 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Category: Summer Concerts\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\t Venue \n\t\n\t\t\t\t Victoria Inner Harbour \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\nInner Harbour\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\tVictoria,\n\n\tBritish Columbia\n\n\tV8W 3M6\n\n\tCanada\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t+ Google Map\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n            Concert Credits\n            SEAN O'LOUGHLINconductorPATRICK CAOpiano\n\n            Supporters\n            Symphony SPLASH! Presenting Sponsor\n\n            \n            Buy Tickets\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t \n\n\t\n\t\n    \n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Navigation\n\t\t\n\t\t\t« The National Youth Orchestra of Canada (SPLASH!)\n\t\t\tKluxen & Leong – Beethoven Violin Concerto »\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t"
      },
