    "https://schema.org/mainContentOfPage": [
      {
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tBroadway and Beyond with Jimmie Herrod\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t20 September 2025 @ 7:30 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWith “a voice like a beacon of hope” (Seattle Times), vocalist Jimmie Herrod earned the rare “Golden Buzzer” recognition on America’s Got Talent in 2021. With a globe-trotting career as a singer, songwriter, and entertainer, he has also toured with Pink Martini since 2017. Making his VS debut, Herrod joins Principal Pops Conductor Sean O’Loughlin and the orchestra for selections from Wicked, Rent, and Les Mis, along with highlights from Bernstein, Sondheim, and more!\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n    \n    Meet the ArtistsFull Concert Program\n    \n    \n        \n    \n        Sean O’Loughlin, conductor\nSean O’Loughlin (b.1972) is the Principal Pops Conductor of the Victoria Symphony and the Principal Pops Conductor of the Syracuse Symphony. His diverse background includes collaborations with some of the leading symphonies and popular artists of today. As a conductor, he has led performances with the Boston Pops Orchestra, the San Francisco Symphony, the Chicago Symphony, the Hollywood Bowl Orchestra, the Minnesota Orchestra, the National Arts Centre Orchestra, the Atlanta Symphony, the Dallas Symphony, the Houston Symphony, the Vancouver Symphony and the San Diego Symphony amongst others. He has served as conductor for symphony tours with Josh Groban, Sarah McLachlan, The Decemberists and the Jerry Garcia Symphonic Celebration. He has appeared on Good Morning America and the PBS Special “Stages” with Josh Groban in addition to NBC’s “A Very Pentatonix Christmas.”\nRecent collaborations include such artists as Alicia Keys, Josh Groban, Journey, a-ha, Jason Mraz, The Beach Boys, Sarah McLachlan, Steven Tyler and Joe Perry, Pentatonix, Kelly Clarkson, Diana Ross, Gladys Knight, Blue Man Group, Janelle Monáe, Audra McDonald, Hall and Oates, the Indigo Girls, The Go-Go’s, Bonnie Raitt, Pink Martini, Brandi Carlile, Weird Al Yankovic, Melissa Etheridge and others. Through his growing number of commissioned and published works, Sean is excited to continue contributing to the rich history of orchestral and wind band literature. His music is published by Excelcia Music, Hal Leonard and Carl Fischer. An annual ASCAP Special Awards winner, Sean was a composition fellow at the Henry Mancini Institute in Los Angeles, and holds composition degrees from New England Conservatory and Syracuse University.\nJimmie Herrod, vocalist\n\nJimmie Herrod is a vocalist, arranger, and composer from Tacoma, Washington living in Portland, Oregon. Jimmie rose to worldwide acclaim on NBC’s America’s Got Talent after receiving the coveted “Golden Buzzer” and ending the competition as a finalist. After his time on television, Jimmie starred in the Las Vegas show America’s Got Talent – Live at Luxor, and competed once more on the spin off series, America’s Got Talent: All-Stars. Jimmie has been seen and heard on Oregon Public Broadcasting; All Classical Portland; as a featured soloist on PBS, including the globally televised Joni Mitchell Songbook concert at The Kennedy Center; toured internationally for seven years with the renowned band Pink Martini, and is regularly featured with major symphonies across the US including the National Symphony Orchestra at the Kennedy Center, San Francisco Symphony, The Cleveland Orchestra, and Houston Symphony to name just a few. Jimmie has released two Eps – his debut “Falling in Love and Learning” and 2022’s “Elated.” Jimmie continues to headline concerts in venues across America in addition to appearances in Paris, France.\n\n    \n\n    \n        Candide – Overture\n(Bernstein)\nCome Rain or Come Shine\n(Arlen/Mercer, arr. Riddle)\nThe Man That Got Away\n(Arlen/Gershwin, arr. Martin)\nThe Boy Next Door\n(Martin/Blane, arr. Ellison)\nHighlights from Wicked\n(arr. Ricketts)\nThe Wizard and I\n(Schwartz)\nINTERMISSION\nRent – Overture\n(arr. O’Loughlin)\nWithout You from Rent\n(arr. O’Loughlin)\nThere Won’t Be Trumpets\n(Sondheim)\nBring Him Home\n(Schönberg, arr. Krogstad)\nSelections from Les Misérables\n(Schönberg, arr. Lowden)\nBoth Sides Now\n(arr. Mendoza)\nMacArthur Park\n(arr. Byess)\n\n    \n\n    \n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAdd to calendar\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tGoogle Calendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tiCalendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook 365\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook Live\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t 20 September 2025 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tstarts at 7:30 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Category: Pops at the Royal\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\t Venue \n\t\n\t\t\t\t Royal Theatre \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n805 Broughton St\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t+ Google Map\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tPhone\n\t\t\t\t\t 250.386.6121 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n            Concert Credits\n            SEAN O'LOUGHLINconductorJIMMIE HERRODvocalist\n\n            Supporters\n            Robert & Devi Jawl Foundation\nSeason UnderwriterA & A King Family Foundation\nPops at the Royal Series UnderwriterSuzanne & John Stewart\nConcert Underwriter\n\n            \n            Buy Tickets\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t \n\n\t\n\t\n    \n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Navigation\n\t\t\n\t\t\t« Inside the Victoria Symphony\n\t\t\tBroadway and Beyond with Jimmie Herrod »\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t"
