  {
    "@id": "https://victoriasymphony.ca/temporary/5c80c932-78c9-4dc4-9f06-f19853269c2b",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/WebPage"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/mainContentOfPage": [
      {
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tM is for Music!\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t13 February 2027 @ 3:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tEight-year-old Sarah T. Murdoch isn’t thrilled about her class trip to the Symphony—no sharks, no climbing wall, not even a frog! But with the help of a conductor and a magical book, she discovers that the orchestra is full of adventure. Through music by Mussorgsky, Barber, Bizet, Saint-Saëns, and John Williams, Sarah learns that symphonic music can move hearts, bodies, and imaginations alike. A fun, participatory concert for children and families.\nNot included in subscription purchase discount.  Tickets available to purchase through the UVic Ticket Centre starting Tuesday, July 21, 2026.\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n    \n    Meet the ArtistsFull Program\n    \n    \n        \n    \n        Shauna Johannesen, writer / performer\nShauna is an award-winning writer, actor, and filmmaker. Her plays have been produced across Western Canada and the short film she wrote, Bedbugs: A Musical Love Story, garnered numerous accolades on the festival circuit, including Leo awards for Screenwriting and Best Female Actor.  Her directorial debut Trying, has likewise earned Johannesen nominations and awards including the Matrix Award for Outstanding Short Work, and the Women in Film and TV Spotlight Image Award.  \nJohannesen’s newest play Common Grace premiered in 2016 at Pacific Theatre and is presently being developed into a feature film. Between writing and directing, she regularly graces your living room via your TV set.  \nShe lives in Vancouver, Canada. \n\n    \n\n    \n        M is for Music, Danderfer\nThe William Tell Overture, Rossini\nNight on the Bald Mountain, Rimsky-Korsakov\nAdagio for Strings, Barber\nLes Toreadors, Bizet\nBaby Shark, Pinkfong\nWest Side Story Selection for Orchestra, Bernstein, Mason\n“Aquarium” from the Carnival of the Animals, Saint-Saëns\nFlight of the Bumblebee, Rimsky-Korsakov\nStar Wars Main Title, Williams\n\n\n    \n\n    \n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAdd to calendar\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tGoogle Calendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tiCalendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook 365\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook Live\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t 13 February 2027 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tstarts at 3:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Category: Kids at the Farquhar\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\t Venue \n\t\n\t\t\t\t Farquhar at UVic \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\nUniversity Farquhar Auditorium, Ring Road\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\tVictoria,\n\n\tBC\n\n\tV8P 5C2\n\n\tCanada\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t+ Google Map\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tPhone\n\t\t\t\t\t 250.721.8480 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n            Concert Credits\n            SHAUNA JOHANNESENwriter / performer\n\n            Supporters\n            Terry Scandrett & Angela Bassage\nSeason Underwriters\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t \n\n\t\n\t\n    \n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Navigation\n\t\t\n\t\t\t« Season Special: Kluxen – Marc-André Hamelin Plays Rachmaninoff’s Piano Concerto No. 3\n\t\t\tBaigent & Crozman – Mozart’s Jupiter & Walton’s Cello Concerto »\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t"
      },
      {
