        "@value": "Appalachian Spring"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "&lt;p&gt;Known for his ability to bring new audiences to the concert hall, the Calgary-born “disruptor-conductor” Daniel Bartholomew-Poyser leads a journey that touches on the beauty of nature and our need to care for our climate. The poetry of Wendy Jean MacLean is set by BC-based choral composer Nicholas Ryan Kelly in Earth, Beloved, a work that...&lt;/p&gt;\\n"
      }
